# `!b&&c||!d`: the `)` that closes `not(b` goes before the ` and` that replaces `&&`.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where !b&&c||!d
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..20
  PIPELINE@0..19
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..19
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..19
        BIN_EXPR@10..15
          PREFIX_EXPR@10..12
            BANG@10..11 "!"
            NAME_REF@11..12
              IDENT@11..12 "b"
          AMP2@12..14 "&&"
          NAME_REF@14..15
            IDENT@14..15 "c"
        PIPE2@15..17 "||"
        PREFIX_EXPR@17..19
          BANG@17..18 "!"
          NAME_REF@18..19
            IDENT@18..19 "d"
  WHITESPACE@19..20 "\n"

error[DS0111]: `!` is not an operator
  --> query:1:11
  |
1 | t | where !b&&c||!d
  |           ^
  |
  = help: negate it with `not(...)`: `not(b)`

error[DS0111]: `&&` is not an operator
  --> query:1:13
  |
1 | t | where !b&&c||!d
  |             ^^
  |
  = help: use `and` to require both conditions

error[DS0111]: `||` is not an operator
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | t | where !b&&c||!d
  |                ^^
  |
  = help: use `or` to accept either condition

error[DS0111]: `!` is not an operator
  --> query:1:18
  |
1 | t | where !b&&c||!d
  |                  ^
  |
  = help: negate it with `not(...)`: `not(d)`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    t | where not(b) and c or not(d)
which parses without errors
